NMR Prediction for Molion
=========================

The plugin's code is under the MIT licence (LICENSE).

The shift table
---------------

data/shifts.bin.gz contains information from nmrshiftdb2 (www.nmrshiftdb.org), which is
made available here under the nmrshiftdb2 Database License:
https://nmrshiftdb.nmr.uni-koeln.de/nmrshiftdbhtml/nmrshiftdb2datalicense.txt

It is a derivative database of nmrshiftdb2 (statistics of measured shifts, grouped by the
surroundings of each atom; see data/SOURCE.md for how it was built) and is distributed under
that same licence. The licence requires software that relies on the database to be released
under an Open Source Initiative-approved licence: this plugin is, under the MIT licence. It is
a separate program from Molion, which talks to it over Molion's plugin protocol and does not
read the table itself.

Method
------

Shifts are predicted with HOSE codes, after W. Bremser, "HOSE — a novel substructure code",
Analytica Chimica Acta 103 (1978) 355–365. The code here is the plugin's own; nothing was
taken from other implementations.
